  "id": "language-pathology",
  "term": "language pathology",
  "definition": "Language pathology is the area of speech-language pathology concerned with how people use and value language in real cultural, linguistic, and social contexts. In this field, language assessment and intervention are understood to affect communication, identity, wellbeing, and access to education and health services.",
